## Submission guidance — read before submitting

Before calling the submit tool, re-read the **Partition** step in the
thinking section above. Decide explicitly:

- **Linear plan.** Stay linear when the steps form a single connected
  thread (one shared template, one test file, one contract touched across
  steps). Do not force `## Work Units` for the sake of parallelism.
- **`## Work Units` plan.** Declare units whenever step groups have
  pairwise disjoint `Files:` lists. Shared contract or interface changes
  belong in one sequential step BEFORE the first unit.

The full Work Units syntax and validator behavior live in
`.agent/artifact-formats/plan.md` and
`ralph/policy/validation/_api.py:validate_work_units_against_policy`. A plan
that declares work units must also fit within the development phase's
`max_parallel_workers` cap.

